1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,590
“He just seems confident, Riya. Hire him.”

2
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:09,368
A 20-minute interview. Rohan smiled at every question… and said “ownership” in every answer.

3
00:00:09,418 --> 00:00:13,848
Sana spoke slowly. But her take-home task? It worked the first time.

4
00:00:13,868 --> 00:00:17,115
And Rohan's task? Still… “almost done”.

5
00:00:17,215 --> 00:00:21,116
Riya's first hiring panel. Argue with the boss… or stay quiet?

6
00:00:21,466 --> 00:00:24,868
Chanakya Niti has the answer… at a goldsmith's counter.

7
00:00:24,968 --> 00:00:30,893
Gold is tested four ways: rubbed, cut, heated… and beaten.

8
00:00:30,943 --> 00:00:35,392
And a person, by four: sacrifice, conduct, qualities… and actions.

9
00:00:35,442 --> 00:00:38,162
Read the list again… “confidence” isn't on it.

10
00:00:38,512 --> 00:00:44,450
So a person is tested by four: sacrifice, conduct, qualities, actions.

11
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:49,580
Research backs the “see the work” part: a work sample predicts the job better than an unstructured interview.

12
00:00:49,630 --> 00:00:55,526
So Riya said: “Sir, we've seen the confidence. Can we see the work? Let's open both tasks together.”

13
00:00:55,676 --> 00:00:58,701
Send this to the manager… who hires on vibes.

14
00:00:58,851 --> 00:01:03,727
Who would you hire: the best talker… or the one whose work you've seen?
